╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [BUG] CrewAI Decorators Don't Support Async Methods - Causes "'coroutine' object has no attribute 'name'" Error                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ### Description                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Summary                                                                                                                                      │
│ CrewAI's `@agent`, `@task`, and `@crew` decorators do not properly support async methods. When decorating async methods that return coroutines, │
│ the decorators fail to unwrap the coroutine, resulting in the error: `'coroutine' object has no attribute 'name'`.                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Environment                                                                                                                                  │
│ - **OS**: Ubuntu 22.04 (Docker)                                                                                                                 │
│ - **Python Version**: 3.13.0                                                                                                                    │
│ - **CrewAI Version**: 0.62.2                                                                                                                    │
│ - **Framework**: FastAPI + Telegram Bot (aiogram) + AsyncSQLAlchemy 2.0                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Description                                                                                                                                  │
│ We're building an async-first architecture where CrewAI crews are executed within FastAPI/Telegram handlers. Tool initialization requires async │
│ database operations via AsyncSession, so we need async tool creation.                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ **Problem Flow:**                                                                                                                               │
│ 1. We decorated agent/task methods with `async def` to support `await self._create_tools()`                                                     │
│ 2. The `@agent`, `@task`, `@crew` decorators don't await the async methods                                                                      │
│ 3. This returns a coroutine object instead of Agent/Task/Crew instances                                                                         │
│ 4. When CrewAI tries to access `.name` attribute on the coroutine, it fails                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Error Stack                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│ ERROR | src.agents.tools.base:run_crew_isolated:141 - Crew execution failed |                                                                   │
│ crew_class=FounderCrew run_mode=answer error='coroutine' object has no attribute 'name'                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Traceback:                                                                                                                                      │
│   File "src/agents/tools/base.py", line 135, in run_crew_isolated                                                                               │
│     result = crew_instance.crew(run_mode).kickoff_async(inputs)                                                                                 │
│ AttributeError: 'coroutine' object has no attribute 'name'                                                                                      │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Workaround Attempted                                                                                                                         │
│ We tried wrapping async `_arun()` calls in a sync `_run()` fallback:                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ def _run(self, *args, **kwargs):                                                                                                                │
│     return run_async(self._arun(*args, **kwargs))  # ❌ Creates new event loop → loop conflicts                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ This reintroduces "Task got Future attached to a different loop" errors because it spawns a new event loop inside the existing one.             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Root Cause Analysis                                                                                                                          │
│ The `@agent`, `@task`, and `@crew` decorators use class method introspection but don't check if the method is a coroutine function. They should │
│ either:                                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1. **Auto-await async methods** (recommended for modern Python):                                                                                │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ def decorator(method):                                                                                                                          │
│     def wrapper(self):                                                                                                                          │
│         result = method(self)                                                                                                                   │
│         if asyncio.iscoroutine(result):                                                                                                         │
│             return asyncio.run(result)  # Or: await result in async context                                                                     │
│         return result                                                                                                                           │
│     return wrapper                                                                                                                              │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 2. **Explicitly reject async methods** with helpful error:                                                                                      │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ def decorator(method):                                                                                                                          │
│     if asyncio.iscoroutinefunction(method):                                                                                                     │
│         raise TypeError(                                                                                                                        │
│             f"Method '{method.__name__}' is async but @agent/@task/@crew "                                                                      │
│             "decorators only support sync methods. "                                                                                            │
│             "Create tools synchronously or use a different pattern."                                                                            │
│         )                                                                                                                                       │
│     return original_decorator(method)                                                                                                           │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Questions for CrewAI Team                                                                                                                    │
│ 1. Are `@agent`, `@task`, `@crew` decorators intentionally limited to sync-only?                                                                │
│ 2. Is there a supported pattern for async tool creation in async-first applications?                                                            │
│ 3. Would a PR adding async support to decorators be welcome?                                                                                    │
│ 4. Should we await async methods at decoration time or at call time?                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Production Context                                                                                                                           │
│ This is a production issue affecting:                                                                                                           │
│ - **Telegram Bot** (aiogram) with async handlers                                                                                                │
│ - **FastAPI** application with async endpoints                                                                                                  │
│ - **AsyncSQLAlchemy** database operations                                                                                                       │
│ - **PostgreSQL** via asyncpg driver                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ We need async-safe tool execution to avoid event loop conflicts and zombie database connections.                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Proposed Solution                                                                                                                            │
│ Add async method detection and auto-await to the decorators:                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ # In crewai/decorators.py or similar                                                                                                            │
│ import asyncio                                                                                                                                  │
│ from functools import wraps                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ def agent(method):                                                                                                                              │
│     @wraps(method)                                                                                                                              │
│     def wrapper(self, *args, **kwargs):                                                                                                         │
│         result = method(self, *args, **kwargs)                                                                                                  │
│         if asyncio.iscoroutine(result):                                                                                                         │
│             # Option 1: Run in current event loop (if in async context)                                                                         │
│             try:                                                                                                                                │
│                 loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()                                                                                               │
│                 # Schedule as task if already in event loop                                                                                     │
│                 return asyncio.ensure_future(result)                                                                                            │
│             except RuntimeError:                                                                                                                │
│                 # No running loop - run new one                                                                                                 │
│                 return asyncio.run(result)                                                                                                      │
│         return result                                                                                                                           │
│     return wrapper                                                                                                                              │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ This allows developers to write naturally async code while maintaining backward compatibility.                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                           │
